{"id": 25, "ts": 1780626650.6124523, "event": "public_discussion_message", "round": 2, "agent": "sarah_mitchell", "message": "I appreciate Emily\u2019s clarification on Candidate\u202fC. While C does indeed foster a positive crew atmosphere and is described as 100\u202f% reliable, the same source flags significant communication challenges\u2014difficulty articulating ideas and an egocentric attitude\u2014that could undermine cockpit coordination, especially on long\u2011haul flights where clear, concise exchange is vital. Moreover, we still lack any concrete evidence of C\u2019s stress\u2011resilience, a non\u2011negotiable criterion for our long\u2011distance routes.\nCandidate\u202fB, on the other hand, demonstrates the core safety pillars we need: \u201cvery conscientious\u201d (operational reliability), \u201chandles stress very well\u201d (stress resilience), and solid technical competence (weather\u2011assessment skill and excellent computer abilities). Although B\u2019s interpersonal style is noted as pretentious, grumpy, and occasionally uncooperative, these are behavioral issues that can be addressed through targeted CRM training and do not outweigh the proven reliability and stress\u2011handling strengths.\nGiven the current evidence, I remain convinced that Candidate\u202fB offers the most balanced fit for the long\u2011distance pilot role, provided we implement focused teamwork and communication coaching."}
